From: xenocideend (with Claude Opus 5.5) <xenocideend@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_pm8150b_charger: fix wakeirq leak on
 remove

The driver has no .remove callback, so the dev_pm_set_wake_irq() call in
probe() is never paired with dev_pm_clear_wake_irq(), and a later
unbind/bind of the driver fails probe() with -EEXIST ("Couldn't set wake
irq"). Use the devm-managed devm_device_init_wakeup() and
devm_pm_set_wake_irq(), as upstream did for the pmi8998 charger.
---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_pm8150b_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_pm8150b_charger.c
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/pm_wakeirq.h>
+#include <linux/pm_wakeup.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/power_supply.h>
 #include <linux/regmap.h>
@@ -946,7 +947,13 @@
 	if (rc < 0)
 		return rc;
 
-	rc = dev_pm_set_wake_irq(chip->dev, chip->cable_irq);
+	/* devm: there is no .remove() to clear the wake irq on unbind */
+	rc = devm_device_init_wakeup(chip->dev);
+	if (rc < 0)
+		return dev_err_probe(chip->dev, rc,
+				     "Couldn't init wakeup source\n");
+
+	rc = devm_pm_set_wake_irq(chip->dev, chip->cable_irq);
 	if (rc < 0)
 		return dev_err_probe(chip->dev, rc, "Couldn't set wake irq\n");
 
